/-! ## Coefficient-sensitivity negative control

A factor with an interior root is genuinely NOT certifiable by this
machinery: `x - 1/2` vanishes at the interior point `x = 1/2`, so a
`facNE`-style lemma for it would be FALSE.  This documents that the
factor lemmas depend on root-freeness on (0,1), not on a vacuous
pattern. -/
example : ∃ x : ℝ, 0 < x ∧ x < 1 ∧ x - 1/2 = 0 :=
  ⟨1/2, by norm_num, by norm_num, by norm_num⟩

